# The table is born empty and is filled under a key that nobody knows. What is stored so is found again by a read under such a key of the same layout, and `push` off what that read gives is still entered though the call has given up, by escape alone: `push` lays what it is handed into its receiver. So of the read Link holds the list, and of the step through it the one function that was pushed.
# f1 = turn, f4 = fire, f5 = the handler
# RUN(HELD): link held accesses mechanisms=all
# HELD: read f4 v5 proven=undefined|Array
# HELD: read f4 v12 proven=undefined|f5
# It is held, not proven: the callee is asked at the run whether it is that function, and behind the question the handler is copied into the loop that fires.
# RUN(FORM): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# FORM-LABEL: code f1:Body
# FORM: frame 1 callee=f4
# FORM: frame 2 callee=f5
# FORM: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=f5
